role in overseeing the certification of gluten-free products across Europe, ensuring that these products comply with strict regulations regarding gluten content. Specifically, FACE is responsible for granting the European License System (ELS) certification for gluten-free products, which guarantees that items bearing its mark contain gluten levels below 10 parts per million (ppm). Through its efforts, FACE aims to enhance the safety and quality of gluten-free options available to consumers.", "CELÍACOS:Las personas celíacas son aquellas que tienen intolerancia al gluten y requieren productos específicos para su dieta.", "GLUTEN:GLUTEN is a protein found in wheat and related grains, including certain cereals. It plays a crucial role in the elasticity of dough, making it important in baking and food production. However, gluten can cause adverse reactions in individuals with celiac disease, a condition that necessitates the complete elimination of gluten from their diet to avoid serious health complications. Additionally, gluten can trigger reactions in those with gluten sensitivity. The certification process for gluten-free products is heavily influenced by the presence of gluten, ensuring that these products meet safety standards for those affected. Recent recommendations from the European Society for Pediatric Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition (ESPGHAN) have also addressed the introduction of gluten into the diets of infants, indicating that guidelines on the timing of gluten introduction have been updated.", "DECLARACIONES NUTRICIONALES:Las declaraciones nutricionales son afirmaciones que sugieren que un alimento tiene propiedades beneficiosas específicas debido a su composición.", "DECLARACIONES DE PROPIEDADES SALUDABLES:Las declaraciones de propiedades saludables afirman o sugieren una relación entre un alimento y la salud.", "DECLARACIONES DE REDUCCIÓN DE RIESGO:Las declaraciones de reducción de riesgo afirman que el consumo de un alimento puede reducir significativamente un factor de riesgo de aparición de una enfermedad.", "REGULACIÓN NUTRICIONAL:", "AOECS:The AOECS, or Association of European Coeliacs, is an organization dedicated to regulating the use of the gluten-free symbol and certifying gluten-free products throughout Europe. It oversees the certification process across its member associations, ensuring that products meet the necessary standards for gluten-free labeling. The AOECS plays a crucial role in supporting individuals with celiac disease by providing assurance regarding the safety and quality of gluten-free products available in the market.", "SPIGA BARRADA:Spiga barrada is the international symbol for gluten-free products, regulated by AOECS and used by industries to signify compliance with gluten-free standards.", "EUROPEAN REGULATIONS:European regulations govern the labeling and production standards for both ecological and organic products across member states. These regulations include specific guidelines for gluten-free certifications, ensuring that products meet established criteria for quality and safety.", "PRODUCTS ECOLOGICAL:Ecological products are those that meet specific European standards for organic production and labeling, including gluten-free requirements.", "GLUTEN-FREE SYMBOL:"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}